    outlook: "The immediate focus will be on the durability of the Israel-Iran ceasefire. Diplomatic channels will be crucial, with the United States expected to play a continuing role in mediation. Concurrently, the world awaits Russia's anticipated offensive in Ukraine, which could trigger a new wave of sanctions from the U.S., UK, EU, Canada, and Australia, and potentially further military aid packages for Kyiv. The United Nations Security Council is likely to convene emergency sessions to address both the Middle East and Ukrainian situations. The outcomes will significantly influence global energy prices, defense spending, and the broader geopolitical alignment of powers. Upcoming G7 and G20 summits will provide platforms for leaders to coordinate responses.",
    conclusion: "The announcement of an Israel-Iran ceasefire by President Trump offers a tentative moment of hope amidst a deeply troubled global landscape. However, the persistent threat of a major Russian offensive in Ukraine and the underlying complexities of Middle Eastern rivalries underscore the precarious balance of international peace. As nations, from India to the United States, navigate these turbulent waters, sustained diplomatic engagement, adherence to international law, and a collective commitment to de-escalation will be paramount in averting further crises and safeguarding global stability.",
