      bearCase: "Persistent high U.S. bond yields could lead to sustained FII outflows, significant INR depreciation, and increased domestic interest rates, severely impacting corporate profitability and investment. Coupled with geopolitical risks and a potential global recession, this could trigger a deep correction in Indian equities and a slowdown in economic growth.",
      neutralCase: "Indian markets will likely experience continued volatility, driven by global yield movements and FII sentiment. While domestic fundamentals remain supportive, external pressures will prevent a sustained upward trajectory. The RBI will likely maintain a cautious stance, balancing inflation and growth, leading to a range-bound market with selective opportunities.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "Our probability-weighted outlook suggests a \'Neutral to Cautiously Bearish\' scenario for Indian equities in the short term (3-6 months). The high probability of sustained U.S. yield pressure (60%) outweighs the bullish domestic factors (40%). While a sharp collapse is unlikely given India\'s resilience, significant upside will be capped by global factors.",
      potentialCatalysts: ["A dovish pivot or clear guidance from the Federal Reserve on future rate hikes.", "Significant de-escalation of geopolitical tensions and improved global risk sentiment.", "Stronger-than-expected corporate earnings in India, signaling resilience.", "Increased domestic institutional investor (DII) buying to offset FII outflows.", "Positive surprises in India\'s macroeconomic data (e.g., lower inflation, higher GDP growth)."],
      keyRisks: ["Continued hawkish stance by the Federal Reserve, pushing U.S. yields even higher.", "Escalation of geopolitical conflicts or new cybersecurity threats impacting global stability.", "Unexpected surge in global commodity prices, fueling inflation.", "Significant slowdown in global economic growth, impacting India\'s exports and capital inflows.", "Any domestic policy missteps or unexpected political instability in India."],
